The Kremlin supports the prohibition of smoking on balconies of residential buildings
the Kremlin supports any measures that will allow to save the lives of people, presidential press secretary Dmitry Peskov said, commenting on the prohibition of smoking on balconies and loggias of apartments.
Earlier, the Cabinet of Ministers approved amendments to the rules of the firing regime, according to which it is forbidden to use an open fire on balconies and rooms of residential buildings.
Subsequently, the Russian Emergencies Ministry reported that we are talking, among other things, about the prohibition of smoking on balconies and loggias of apartments and hotels.
The changes will come into force from October 1, 2019.
For violation, administrative responsibility is provided.
The Kremlin has a positive attitude towards any solutions that help save human lives.
“We know how many of the fires occur, many of them have very tragic consequences and public resonance.
Therefore, any saved life justifies such decisions,” Peskov said.
In the first place, the spokeswoman evaluates this as a fire-fighting measure, and not a way to protect its neighbors from tobacco smoke.
Peskov also noted that the President of Russia Vladimir Putin does not welcome smoking and is a supporter of a healthy lifestyle.
Gattuso is looking for work in one of the Russian clubs
Italian football coach Gennaro Gattuso arrived in Russia in order to search for a new club.
According to “Championship”, the 41-year-old specialist flew to Moscow to study the opportunity to find a job in some Russian club.
Gatatuzo’s previous place of work was “Milan” which he headed from 2017 to 2018, which under his leadership took the fifth place in the tournament table of the Italian Serie A and was not able to go to the Champions League.
As a trainer, he also worked in the Swiss “Syon”, the Greek “OFIs”, as well as Italian “Palermo” and “Pizea”.
Earlier it was reported that Pavel Mamaev’s negotiations with “Dynamo” under the threat of failure.
The ex-coach “Milan” arrived in Moscow in order to lead the Russian club
The former player of the national team of Italy and the former head coach of “Milan” Gennaro Gattuso flew to Moscow in order to lead the Russian club.
Gattuzo is the world champion of 2006 as part of the Italian national national team.
At the clubal level, he was known for his performances for Milan, with whom he twice won the UEFA Champions League in 2003 and 2007.
The Italian began his coaching career in Cyon.
Over the last two seasons Gennaro led Rossoneri.
