The Ministry of internal Affairs of Russia proposes to be punished for insulting the police on the Internet
The Ministry of internal Affairs of Russia has prepared amendments to the law “On police” in order to to protect guards of order from the dissemination of defamatory and disgraciating information on the Internet.
On the federal portal of normative legal acts there was an application for a public discussion of the bill, the draft document itself has not yet been published.
The explanatory note to the document notes that it is being developed in connection with the need to protect the honesty and meaning of a police officer from “distributing in information and communication networks, including in the “Internet network”, defamatory information, including those of a discrediting nature.
Exactly how it is planned to protect the police from slandering in the network, is not specified.
At the same time in the explanatory note to the document it is noted that the provisions of the amendments will be applied "by individualization of the mechanism already provided for by the law on the blocking of posts that offend government officials and the law on fines for such posts.
Both laws came into force in March this year.
The final text of the bill will be published after public discussions and an independent anti-corruption examination.
In accordance with the explanatory note, the amendments to the law “On police” should enter into force in January 2020.
March 18 President Vladimir Vladimir Putin signed a law on punishment for “clear disreprudence to the state” on the Internet.
According to this document, Roskomnadzor warns the resource about the violation and gives him a day to eliminate it.
For the first violation of the prohibition, a fine in the amount of 30 to 30 to 300 thousand rubles is provided, and for a repeated infringement - an administrative arrest for a period of up to 15 days.
On April 12, Roskomnadzor for the first time applied this norm against the media, having blocked the Yaroslavl edition 76.ru.
Shortly thereafter, the Chudovsky district court of the Novgorsk region fined a local inhabitant of 30 thousand rubles for the fact that he placed in the network “two entries with information in an inaccessible form, which offends human dignity and public morality and expresses an obvious disrespect to the society, the state, bodies exercising state power in the Russian Federation”.
Named the period of reduction of mortgage rates
Rates on housing loans in Russia will be reduced until the end of 2019.
This was stated by the General Director of the credit organization “Dom.rf” Alexander Plutnik, reports “Interfax”.
As Plutnik noted at the board under the Ministry of Construction of Russia, the majority of the banks in the remaining months of the year will hold another cycle of reducing mortgage rates, and the market average will reach 8.9 per cent - the level provided for by the national project "Housing and Urban Environment".
according to the passport of the project, in 2019 the average mortgage rate should be 8.9 percent, in 2021 - 8.5 per cent, by 2024 - 7.9 percent.
The program envisages “the provision of affordable housing for families with medium-scouple, including the creation of opportunities for the purchase of housing using a mortgage, the bet of which must be less than 8 per cent).
Earlier in September it became known that one of the largest players of the Russian mortgage market - Sberbank - is planning until the end of 2019 to carry out another reduction in rates for housing loans.
Will phytoestrogens and phytopandrogens help prolong their youth
Phytopandrogen is poorly explored.
Of the most well-known - pine pollen.
But phytoestrogens are well-expelled and have a positive effect on the body.
They reduce the risks of certain age-associated diseases associated with age (among them cardiovascular, certain types of cancer).
Familiar sources of phytoestrogens - all beans (the most popular - sonia), hops, flax see seeds.
However, many experts believe that such dietary DIA can not act as a proper replacement for natural hormones.
Possible damage from such add-ons cannot be eliminated.
For example, against the background of their intake, the production of their own hormones may decrease due to the fact that there are too many analogues from the outside entering the body.
