There is no need for Russians to retrieve - V. Matviyenko
The representative of the Federation Council Valentina Matvienko believes that the Russians do not have sufficient savings in order to in the country to fully work a bill on a guaranteed pension product.
The practice of increasing the pension due to personal accumulators in the world is quite prevalent.
It’s another matter how timely its introduction we have.
“In my opinion, now a significant part of the population has income, of which they simply have nothing to allocate to an increase in pension provision in the future,” Matvienko said.
The Russians, according to the speaker, can not understand the mechanisms for the formation and accrual of a pension, since “permanent changes in this area are finally confused.”
It doesn't mean I'm against improving the pension system that regulates its legislation.
“Russia is a social state, and we are obliged to do everything in order to ensure that the size of pensions, social security of citizens improve.
But the steps in this direction should be thoughtful, responsible, taking into account domestic realities," Matviyenko told RIA Novosti.
The Chairman of the Federation Council stressed that if this initiative (the bill on a guaranteed pension product) will be developed, then several basic principles must necessarily be provided, including voluntonishness, tax preferences for citizens and employers and strict guarantees and the responsibility of the state to ensure the safety of pension savings.
The Ministry of Finance of the Russian of the Russian Federation on September 6 announced the sending for approval of the bill on a guaranteed pension product (GPP).
Among its main elements - an exclusively voluntary procedure for uniting citizens to the system of savings, guaranteeing the preservation of long-term pension savings of citizens from the state, registration of accumulative bills of citizens by the central administrator, tax benefits for business and tax deductions for citizens.
Spider-Man Remains in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.
Sony and Disney Have Arrived
Getty Images Image caption The news about the departure of the beloved superhero from the Marvel film universe has angered many loyal admirers
One of the most notorious communicative communicators - Spider-Man - will remain in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.
The companies of Disney and Sony Pictures managed to agree on the rights to its use in the films of the franchise.
About it became known from the press release of Sony, in which it is said that the third part of “Spider-Man” with Tom Holland will be released on July 16, 2021.
Earlier it was reported that Disney and Sony Pictures could not come to a consensus on the division of income, because of which Spider-Man will leave the Marvel Cinematic Universe.
The rights to the movie hero are owned by Sony.
She leased them for the Marvel movies, which is owned by Disney.
As a Rescue, Sony received income from revenue in the box office, and Disney with souvenirs and toys.
As it is reported, at some point this situation has ceased to suit Disney, and the company wanted to revise the agreement.
The President of Marvel Studios, Kevin Feigi said that he was delighted.
Amazing that Spaidi’s voyage in the marvel will continue.
“All of us at Marvel Studios are delighted that we will be able to continue to work on it.
Spider-Man is ignorant figure.
This is a hero, whose history touches all generations and audience audiences around the world”, – stated in his press release.
At the same time, Feigi recalled that Sony is also creating its own movie universe, built just around Spider-Man.
So it happened that he is the only self-educated hero who finds himself in different movie universes.
So, as long as Sony continues to develop its own Spidery-universe, the future can present unexpected surprises,” he said. – he said.
Tom Holland, who played Spider-Man in five films, apparently, commenting on the news, posted in his Instagram account an passage from the film “Woolf with Wall Street”, in which Leonardo DiCaprio shouts “I don’t leave!”
information about the contradictions between the companies appeared in August.
As reported by the media, Disney wanted to receive half the box office proceeds from films about Spider-Man, on the condition that both companies will pay for the cost of producing paintings.
That didn’t like Sony.
The news about the possible departure of the beloved superhero from the Marvel Cinema has angered many dedicated fans.
Destinies of new conditions have not yet been disclosed.
According to CNBC reports, Sony refused to comment on the agreement, but said: “We have cooperated well for the last four years, and our joint desire to continue working together was commensurate with the wishes of many Spider-Men.
We are delighted that we can move forward together.”
