Van Yi met with UN Secretary-General A. Guterrish
Member of the State Council and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China Wang Yi on Thursday met with UN Secretary-General António Guterres at the UN headquarters in New York.
According to Gautterish at the meeting, China plays an extremely important role in creating a multipolar world.
The UN is grateful to the Chinese government for its powerful support and fertile cooperation, and highly appreciates the important contribution made by China made to the international fight against poverty, combating climate change and creating a green Belt and Path.
He wants to deepen cooperation with China in the field of protection of security and peace and sustainable development, and also hopes that China will continue to play a leading role in the fight against climate and other areas.
Wan Yi, in turn, noted that multipolarity is an unavoidable trend, and every country has the right to develop.
Implementing multipolarity is impossible without multilateralism, the symbols of which are the main goals and principles established in the UN Charter.
According to the Minister, China stands in favor of a more active role of the UN, supports the work of the Secretary-general of the world organization and strictly adheres to the basic ideas and principles of the UN Charter.
Next year there will be a celerated 75-th anniversary of the founding of the United Nations, and the Chinese side intends to use this opportunity to strengthen cooperation with the global organization in order to jointly create a beautiful future for the whole of the world.
