The expert explained why it is worth abandoning the tea in the savages
A group of scientists from Canada, representing McGuyll University, found that when brewing a medge of a medge of Tea in a cup in five minutes gets more than ten billion particles of microplastics.
Diepissolete particles can also be added to a packaged drink, food safety expert Elizaveta Tikhonova told Nation.
According to the agronomist, the consumer can not get reliable information about the composition of packaged tea - the manufacturer can add ingredients that will not be indicated on the packaging.
Sawmiderments at the end of the season do not discard, so they can end up in tea.
“Moreover, tea plants don’t always turn into bags,” Tikhonova said.
According to her, it is better to abandon the use of such a drink in favor of tea on the weight, which is sold in specialized stores.
In addition, she stressed that the hazard of packaged tea lies not only in the composition, but also in the method of its production - microparticles are heated to high temperatures, because of which they can start releasing harmful substances.
It is best to purchase pure green or black tea - in such a drink there will be the least additives", - the expert said.
The problems of the development of the Arctic will be discussed at an international conference in Norilsk
The problems of development of the Arctic will be discussed at an international conference in Norilsk.
