The regions proposed to share the secrets of business support
As it became known "Parliamentary Gazeta", on September 27, the Chairman of the Federation Council Committee on Economic Politics Andrei Kutepov sent a letter to the minister of economic development Maxim Oreshkin and Finance Minister Anton Siluanov with a proposal to express a position regarding the initiatives of the subjects of the Federation to improve legislation to support small and medium-sized entrepreneurship (SME).
It's time to establish inter-regular relations
The Committee of the Federation Council on Economic Policy summarized the information received from the regions about the programs for the development of business and the legalization of self-occupied, as well as on the results of such programs.
In their letters the regions told senators about the problems of the development of SMEs and sent proposals to improve the current legislation.
“To the present day, communication between the regions has not been sufficiently established, as a result, as a result, as a result, the business community in all regions visits by senators outlined the issue of lack of information about regional entrepreneurship development programs in the whole country,” Andrey Kutepov said.
In the appendix to the letter, which was sent to the Government, he presented a set of positive developments of the regions for the legalization of self-employment and consolidated data from the regions with proposals and problems (available to the editorial board).
In addition to relevant ministries, consolidated data from the regions was also sent to the heads of the regional executive authorities.
The exchange of information about positively implemented developments in the regions could give impetus to the development of entrepreneurship as a whole.
The first step towards such an exchange will be the provision of information available to the Economic Policy Committee," the senator told the Parliamentary Newspaper.
Wealthy experience
Today in many regions of the country adopted and successfully operate programs to support small and medium-sized businesses.
For example, in the Vologda region there is a entrepreneurship support center, which, in addition to financial support measures, assists businessmen in the certification of finished products.
In the Ivanovo region has developed a business support system, providing for the implementation of the principle of a single window through multifunctional centers.
In the Krasnodar Krai, novice agricultural consumer cooperatives are provided with grants at the expense of the regional budget.
In the Oryol region there is a cluster development center.
The Amur region in the framework of the federal project "Acceleration of small- and medium-sized entrepreneurship entities" envisages the possibility of subsidizing business incubators created on the basis of existing non-state coworking centers at the expense of the federal budget.
And in a number of other regions, special support measures are being taken for youth entrepreneurship.
Self-employed continue to get out of the shadow
According to the regional authorities, in order to more effectively support small and medium-sized businesses, a number of changes should be made to the current legislation.
For example, the Arkhangelsk region proposed to replace the term "self-employment" with "enterprising activities", since this "most corresponds to the content of the state service to promote self-employment of unemplified citizens."
In the Ivanovo region it is considered it necessary to make amendments, providing for the expansion of a list of activities provided by self-emplified citizens, including the types of activities for finishing and refurbishment of residential premises, suburban buildings, conducting physical training.
Bryansk region considers it important to strengthen control over unscrupulous producers of dairy products with the veterinary system "Mercury".
In Kostroma and Magadan regions, they are advocating the concept of “social entrepreneurship” and areas for supporting social entrepreneurship in the regulatory legal field.
All proposals from the regions will be taken into account when preparing state programs to support small and medium-sized entrepreneurship, and the most important will receive development in the form of specific bills.
“All proposals from the regions will be taken into account when preparing state programs to support small and medium-sized entrepreneurship, and the most important will receive development in the form of concrete bills,” Andrei Kutepov assured.
The airline helped the passengers to avoid the neighbourhood with crying children
Air carrier Japan Airlines (JAL) has launched a new feature: when booking seats on the plane, you can now find out where the small children will stay.
Now you can be avoided if there is a desire for neighbourhood with them.
Passengers of the Japanese airline Japan Airlines (JAL) have the opportunity to take advantage of a new option and avoid an undesirable neighbility with young children.
The air carrier has launched a function that allows you to track in which places the children will sit.
When selecting places in the salon during booking of tickets, passengers will be able to see the child's head in the field, which are occupied by children aged from eight days to two years.
Thus, those who do not want to fly next to the babies due to the possible inconvenience associated with their censure can stay as far away from them as possible.
Internet users, who use the services of the airline, were delighted with the innovation.
Some of them thanked the carrier, noting that other airlines should do the same way.
One of the users complained that a few weeks ago he was flying from New York to Doha, and in the neighborhood with him there were three weeping children at once.
Another commentator proposed to introduce "fives only for adults", expressing a willingness to pay for such a flight.
Many tourists noted that now they will always try to always choose Japan Airlines for their movements, since they do not see anything pleasant in flying next to a weeping child in an enclosed space.
Earlier, the woman, traveling with the baby, tried to appease fellow travelers during the flight Seoul - San Francisco.
She prepared for each of the 200 passengers a sac with sweets, in each of which there was an apology note.
Oleg Tabakov's Train appeared in the capital's subsidiary?
If you constantly use the Kaluga-Rizh line (and the majority of Konkov residents do so), then a surprise awaits you.
In the subway launched a new themed train "Great Russian artist Oleg Tabakov".
Every day this nominal composition is carried by 10 thousand people.
He handles just on the orange line and talks about the director, actor and the founder of the theater "Tobacco".
By the way, from Konkov it is convenient to go to performances, which are played on the new stage of the theater (it is located on Malaya Sukharevskaya square, next to the Sukharevskaya metro station).
As explained to us in the press service of the Moscow metro, "in the external design of the the thematic train, images of fragments of stained-glabs of a new stage are used and portraits of Oleg Tabakov in the iconic images he created in the theater, cinema and animation are placed."
The train tells the story of his family, the spectacle "Sailor's Silence", from which a great life of the theater began, about "Tobacco", about the director's work.
On the walls of the cars you can see rare archival pictures and footage from the movies.
Russian Gehes with Adopted Babies Receipt Receipt of Asylum in U.S.
An same-sex couple of Russians with two adopted children requested asylum in the United States, reports RIA Novosti.
It is reported that the men left the Russian Federation for Ukraine, and then went to the United States, where they applied for asylum.
According to the Stimul group, the basis for such actions of the family was “incessant interest from law enforcement agencies”.
It is reported that the men do not plan to return to Russia.
Since the beginning of the educational year, children have been studying in an American school and are adapting to new conditions.
We will remind, earlier it was reported about the initiation of a case against the employees of the Department of social protection of the population of the Maryino district because of the adoption by a same-sex family of two young boys.
The HRC at the same time stated that the upbringing of their children a same-sex couple in itself should not become a reason for the initiation of a case.
In the press-center MIC "Izvestia" there will be a press-secret conference of the project of the Moscow Art Theater "SEASON POINTS Third St. Poetry"
October 3 at 11-:00 in the press-center MIC "Izvestia" there will be an annointing press conference: The start of the project "SEASON OF POINTS: The Third Stage. Poetry" in the Moscow-Gorky Moscow Art Theater.
Eduard Boyakov, artistic director of the Moscow State Technical Assembly named after M. Gorky, director of the project.
Ivan Kupreyanov, the poet, the producer of the project.
Dmitry Vodennikov, the poet.
Irina Lindt, actress of theater and cinema.
Aleksey Shmelev, poet.
In the new season, the third stage of the Moscow State Technical Council named after M. Gorky will become a territory of total poetry.
As part of an extensive program, spectacles will be shown, which are based on the poems of the main poets of our time.
The design team will create for the viewers a unique poetic world of verses, music and multimedia images.
The artistic director of the Moscow Art Theater Eduard Boyakov and the curator of the project, poet and producer Ivan Kupriyanov will present the first and only theatrical anthologie of modern elegant literature - the project "SEASON OF POINTS: A Third Scene. Poetry".
The season opens on October 5 at 19:00 on the Third Stage of the Gorky Moscow Art Theater with a spectacle of a poet-legend, whose performance becomes a significant event for connoisseurs of figurative liquourt, Dmitry Vodennikov.
Phoulets will take place in October and November.
Each spectacle is its own author, curator and actor.
The performances will be attended by artists of the Moscow Art Theater and invited stars: Irina Lindt, Agnia Kuznetsova, Olga Kabo, Alisa Grebenshchikov.
The musical concept of the project - Sergey Letov.
The curators in the spectacle will perform: Pavel Kryuchtkov, Maria Golovanivskaya, Eduard Boyakov, Ivan Kupriyanov, etc.
The project is carried out with the support of the Ministry of Culture of the Russian Federation.
Pavel Ustinov joined the pickets in support of the defendants of the “Moscow case”
The actor Pavel Ustinov joined a series of solitary pickets “Freedom to everyone”, which take place on Friday near the building of the presidential administration of the Russian Federation on the Old square in Moscow, the correspondent of “Interfax”.
A series of pickets began on September 18 in support of Ustinov himself and has since continued every day.
At the present time, the participants of the action, replacing each other, stand, holding a poster with the inscription “Security to everyone” and cherries of convicts and arrested after uncoordinated rallies in the summer of 2019.
In addition to Ustinov, on the poster the names of Yegor Zhukov, Kirill Zhukov, Danil Begleza, Evgenia Kovalenko, Konstantin Kotov, Ivan Podkopaev, Aydar Gubaidulina, Alexei Minyaylo, Sergei Fomin, Samariddin Rajabov, Nikita Chirtsov, Eduard Malyshevsky, Vladislav Sinitsa.
The Tver court of Moscow on September 16 sentenced the 24-year-old Ustinov to 3.5 years in a general-regime colony on charges of applying violence against a riot policeman of Rosgvartiya at an uncoordinated action on August 3 in the center of Moscow (part 2 of article 318 of the criminal Code of the Russian Federation).
After that, on September 20 at the request of the General Prosecutor’s office, the court amended Ustinov the measure of restraint from detention for a recognizance of not re-receiving.
So, the petition for the release of Ustinov scored more than 112 thousand signatures per day.
The artists of theater and cinema began a flash mob in the support of a colleague.
To participate in solitary picket as a sign of solidarity with the actor on September 18, a queue was lined up on the Old Square.
Revision of the case was demanded by human rights activists, journalists, scientists, teachers, doctors, Orthodox Priests.
As reported to “Interfax” Sister Ustinova Yulia, at the rally on September 29 in the capital in support of the defendants of the “Moscow case”, her brother does not plan to speak.
Deliveries “sanctions” in Russia fell by 100 times
The government of the Russian Federation estimates that the supply of agricultural products and food to Russia from countries that fell under the Russian food embargo has decreased by more than 100 times since 2013.
According to the report sent to the President of the Russian Federation Vladimir Putin, in the first half of 2019, 31 thousand tons of products were imported from the sanctions countries against 3 million 442.2 thousand tons for the same period in the same period of 2013, reports “Interfax”. “Interfax”.
At the same time, the cost of imported products decreased to $ 226.5 million from $ 4 billion 975.5 million, respectively.
We are talking about the supply of goods, which did not fall under an embargo.
As stated in the report, lost volumes of prohibited products were compensated by an increase in imports from the countries of the CIS, Africa, South-Coastal Asia and Serbia.
Recall that at the end of August, the government promonstrated until December 31, 2020 the validity of the rules for the destruction of agricultural products, raw materials and food, which are prohibited for import into Russia as part of counter-sanctions.
In the document, published on the official portal of legal information, it was notorimated that the validity of the rules has been extended for another one for a year - from December 31, 2019 to December 31, 2020.
Initially, the decree on the destruction of the sanctions applied to products from the United States, the EU, Australia, Norway and Canada.
Subsequently, from August 13, 2015, this list "joined" Albica, Montenegro, Island, Lichtenstein, from January 1, 2016 - Ukraine.
The decree signed by Putin to exterminate the “sanquility” illegally imported into the country (the food embargo, which Moscow imposed in response to anti-Russian Western sanctions) came into force in 2015.
In turn, the government allowed to destroy “sanctional” food in any legal way.
As Western Sanctions Responsible, Russia also extended its responsive strife.
At the same point of this measure does not apply to the products that citizens are imported for personal use.
The prohibition does not concern the import of goods for personal consumption weighing up to 5 kilograms.
However, the head of the Council under the President of the Russian Federation for the development of civil society and human human rights Mikhail Fedotov previously called “simply memorable” the destruction of food, and this, according to him, negatively affects the upbringing of people.
Moreover, Rospotrebnadnadzor made an initiative to prohibit the destruction of food suitable for consumption in early June.
After that, a similar recommendation to the government was given by the Human Rights Council under the President of the Russian Federation.
Deputy Prime Minister Alexei Gordeyev said that it is wrong to destroy food, and it is necessary to think how you can use them for its intended purpose, appreciating the quality.
The head of the company was found guilty of evasion of tax evasion
By the veripulation of the Leninsky district court of Cheboksary, the Director of LLC "Earth and Law" Vyacheslav Morozov was found guilty of committing the crimes provided for paragraph "b" of part 2 of article 199 of the Criminal Code of the RUSSIAN thieves (evasion from payment of taxes from the organization by including knowingly false information, committed on an especially large scale) and part 2 of article 327 of the Criminal Code of the RUSSIAN thievance (forger of an official
This is reported by the press service of the Investigative Department of the Investigative TFR in Chuvashia.
From January 2008 to December 2009, Vyacheslav Morozov entered information about imperfect transactions in the tax accounting documents LLC.
According to fictitious documents, the company incurred additional costs, and, consequently, the value-announced taxes to be payable and 11.2 million ruble on the profit of the organization were reduced.
Vyacheslav Morozov was punished in the form of 3.5 years in prison on probation.
By 2023 in the center of the capital will open the first school of a new format
The school of the new sample will be opened in Khamovniki.
According to the head of Moskomstroyinvest Anastasia Pyatova, there will create all the conditions for self-actualization and the development of children’s talents.
The educational institution decided to call a “new look”.
This project will be supervised by the Moscow State Institute of International Relations of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Foreign Ministry and the Fund "Economic development of higher education".
To the design of the building with an area of about 10 thousand "squares" are planned to begin next year.
The construction will be completed at the end of 2022, and in the next will begin to recruit the first students.
“The project envisages the creation of an accessible, non-commercial educational space, which will be based on the traditions of the classical Moscow school and experimental methods”, – said the press service of Moskomstroyinvest.
In Chile began to build a telescope worth 1 billion euros
About it reports TASS with reference to the press service of the European Southern observatory (ESO).
According to ESO, this week officially began construction of the dome of the building, which will be located Telescope (European Extremely Large Telescope), while the most expensive and ambitious terrestrial astronomical project.
Its total cost, according to ESO estimates, will exceed a billion euros.
Most of this money will be spent on the manufacture of equipment and the construction of an observatory building.
The most expensive and complex component of the telescope - its record-breaking large mirror, whose diameter will be about 39 meters.
It will be harvested from 798 hexagonal dimensions of 1.4 meter in size.
This is a huge mirror, as well as two auxiliary reflectors with a diameter of 4.2 and 3.75 meter, will help E-ELT to obtain the first detailed photos of planets outside the solar system, stars in other galaxies, as well as to look for doppelgangers of the Earth.
In addition, the scientists will try to use this observatory to obsolete Sgr A*, an ultra-massive black hole at the center of the Milky Way.
Despite the fact of the fact that the construction of the dome has just begun, mirrors, scientific instruments and other components of the observatory scientists, engineers and other specialists have been developing for more than three years - from the date of the announcement of the first plans for the construction of E-ELT.
The contract for the production of the main mirror, whose cumulative value amounted to about 400 million euros, was received by the German company SCHOTT and the French company Safran Reosc.
